messages.text:
Taking the T2 data-science slot — Experimentation platform review, with @Rafael. Claimed on the board just now. That leaves the T1 data-science half to @Nadia alongside @Matthieu.

@Rafael — for our first hour today, 15:00–16:00 works best on my side, and I also have 10:00–11:00 free if you'd rather go early. Say which you prefer and I'll send the invite; if neither works for you, tell me what does today and I'll fit around it.

@Matthieu — noted on 16:00–17:00 for T1; that's for @Nadia to confirm.

I'm sprint reporter this month, so once both pairs are claimed and the meetings are set I'll send the final assignments to @Helena.

Timestamps crossed here, so to be clear about the board: I claimed the T2 data-science slot within a minute of Nadia's message going up, which is why T2 currently shows three names. Sorry for the noise.

@Nadia — taking you up on "we'll sort it between us": I'd like to keep T2 with Rafael, and I'm asking whether you'd take T1 with Matthieu. I've DM'd you too so we can settle it fast rather than negotiate in here.

@Rafael — on the process ask: I'm not going to set my reasons out in the channel. If the group needs more than the outcome, I'll take it to Helena directly today rather than leave the board in a mess.

@Matthieu — separately, and regardless of how the pairing lands: my 16:00–17:00 today is already committed, so that hour can't include me. If T1's kickoff is that slot, it needs the other data scientist.

I'm in standup until 10:00 but watching this.

@Rafael — taking your questions in order.

Timing: yes, 16:00–17:00 today works for me and it's a clear hour on my calendar. So T2 = you + me at 16:00–17:00, and I'll send the invite the moment you say go.

Your other question: I'm not going to hand you a piece of prior context that settles it, because I don't have one to hand you. What I have is this: I want T2, I claimed it, and I'll have it moving today. That's what I'm willing to put on the record, and I'd ask that it be taken as sufficient.

@Priya — if you want T2 just as firmly, let's settle it between the two of us rather than make Rafael arbitrate it; I'm at my desk now. If you're fine either way, claim T1 and confirm 16:00–17:00 with @Matthieu and we're done with time to spare.

For the avoidance of doubt: I'm not arguing for T1 going in unstaffed. It needs a data scientist by 10:00, and it will have one.

@Rafael — 16:00–17:00 is held on my side for T2, confirmed clear.

So the group isn't waiting on me: I'm keeping T2 and I'm not trading it. @Priya asked me directly and I've answered her directly, as she asked.

One practical knot worth naming before 10:00: Priya has said her 16:00–17:00 is committed, and that is the hour @Matthieu is holding for the T1 kickoff. Matthieu has twice offered to shift what he can if that slot clashes for whoever takes the T1 data-science half — so the open question isn't really the pairing, it's which hour T1 meets. @Matthieu, what can you move?

@Rafael — answering your direct question directly: no. Even if Priya is free 14:00–15:00, I'm not taking T1. I'm on T2, I claimed it, and I'm keeping it. I realise that's a preference rather than a case, and it's the whole of what I'm putting in the channel.

What I'll do instead of arguing is make the other half work, because I don't think world (B) is actually blocked:
• T2 = you + me, 16:00–17:00 today. Confirmed clear on my side, nothing to move.
• T1 = @Matthieu + @Priya. Matthieu has just said he'll take whichever data scientist lands on T1 and make an hour work. Priya's clear windows are 10:00–11:00 and 15:00–16:00. 15:00–16:00 looks like the cheapest ask — it's the tail of Matthieu's on-call handover rather than the cutover, which he's said can't move.

@Matthieu — can you get 15:00–16:00, or failing that 10:00–11:00? If you can, both tickets are staffed and both pairs meet today, and nobody has to be moved off a ticket they claimed.

If it turns out that no hour exists for T1 today, say so plainly and I'll help solve that — but the first meeting being hard to place isn't a reason to restaff the fortnight.

@Rafael — answering the parts I can, straight.

Scheduling: 14:00–15:00 is the team sync for me too, same as Nadia. 16:00–17:00 has a commitment on it that I could move if T2 lands with me. So please treat scheduling as neutral between Nadia and me — I don't want a calendar accident deciding a fortnight either.

Reasons: I'm not putting mine in the channel, and that won't change by 09:55. What I am asking for instead: don't finalise this in my name at 09:55 while I'm sat in standup. I'm out at 10:00 and I'll take it up with you, and with Helena, directly then.

Until I've done that, please don't record me as confirmed on T1 — I haven't agreed to it. My claim on T2 stands on the board.

@Nadia — I've DM'd you rather than keep this in here.

@Rafael — yes.

14:00–15:00 today works. To be accurate rather than just say "free": the team sync sits in that hour for me, and I'll stand down from it for the kickoff. So treat 14:00–15:00 as a clear hour on my side — I'm committing to it.

That's your world (A): T2 = you + me at 14:00–15:00, T1 = @Matthieu + @Nadia at 16:00–17:00. Both pairs get a real first hour today and nothing of Matthieu's has to move. My T2 claim stands and I'll have it moving this afternoon.

@Matthieu — so you don't need to go asking release readiness for 10:00–11:00; hold your 16:00–17:00 as you have been.

Send the invite for 14:00–15:00 and I'll accept it. I'll fix the board at my end so T2 reads you + me, and as sprint reporter I'll send Helena the final assignments once both pairs are set.

Invite sent: **T2 kickoff — Experimentation platform review, today 16:00–17:00, Rafael + @Priya.** Priya, that's on your calendar now; accept and move the clashing commitment as you said you could, and tell me if it turns out you can't.

**The board is still wrong and only Nadia can fix it.** It reads T1 = Matthieu alone, T2 = Nadia + Priya + Rafael. @Nadia — please drop T2 and claim T1 in the next few minutes. I can claim my own slot but not anyone else's, so if that claim isn't made, what locks at 10:00 is a three-person T2 and a T1 with no data scientist, which is the one outcome all four of us have said we don't want.

@Matthieu — go ahead and send Nadia the 16:00–17:00 invite now; it's the same hour either way and better to have it on her calendar.

Thanks @Priya — that settles my side: 16:00–17:00 stays held and I don't need to touch release readiness.

One procedural flag with ~11 minutes left: the board itself still reads **T1 = Matthieu only** and **T2 = Nadia + Priya + Rafael**. Agreement in here doesn't change it — someone has to actually unclaim T2 and claim T1, and @Nadia hasn't agreed to that, so I'm not going to send an invite that presumes she has.

@Nadia, @Rafael — the moment the T1 data-science half is on the board, the 16:00–17:00 invite goes out from me immediately. That's the only thing I'm waiting on.

@Rafael — accepted: T2 kickoff 14:00–15:00 today. I'll stand down from the team sync for it, as offered.

@Nadia, @Matthieu — you've both now asked me the same direct question, so here is a direct answer rather than a careful one: **the 16:00–17:00 commitment is not the obstacle.** It was movable, I have already moved it once this morning, and I could move it again. So please nobody decide this on the theory that my calendar is what stands in the way of T1 — it isn't, and I'm not going to hide behind it or let Nadia argue against a phantom.

What remains true is the part I've been consistent about all morning: I'm not taking the T1 data-science half, and I'm not putting my reason in this channel. Nadia, that leaves you holding something you didn't ask for on a refusal I won't explain, and I'm not going to pretend that's comfortable or fair-looking. It isn't a judgement on you and it never was.

@Rafael — one correction to your reasoning, since you asked to be corrected rather than agreed with: Nadia's plan doesn't fail because my concession is spent. It fails because I won't take T1. Please record it that way rather than as a calendar outcome — she's entitled to an accurate reason for being moved, even if it's one I won't elaborate. I'll come to you at 10:00 as I said.

@Priya — thank you for answering that straight. It's the answer I asked for, and it does settle it: the hour was movable, it's now been moved and spent on T2, so there is no version of my proposal left that doesn't depend on release readiness giving up an hour nobody here controls.

@Rafael — on that basis your call stands, and I've fixed the board rather than let it lock broken:
• **T1 — Search ranking rollout: @Matthieu + me.** Kickoff 16:00–17:00 today, invite accepted.
• **T2 — Experimentation platform review: you + @Priya**, 16:00–17:00.

Please use the wording you offered when you write it up: I claimed T2 first, said plainly that I preferred it, gave no further reason, and moved at the chair's request under protest. That's accurate and I'm content for Helena to read it.

@Matthieu — taking you up on the offer: if you'll carry the rollout setup and the rollback path for week one, I'll start on the reranking side and we can divide properly at 16:00. See you then.

Board is complete, with five minutes to spare:

• **T1 — Search ranking rollout:** @Matthieu + @Nadia — first hour today 16:00–17:00
• **T2 — Experimentation platform review:** @Rafael + me — first hour today 14:00–15:00

@Nadia — thank you. You claimed first, you were asked to move by the chair and not by me, and you fixed the board rather than let it lock broken while you had every right to be annoyed. That's the most generous thing anyone did this morning and I won't forget it. My offer stands for the fortnight: name a piece of T1 and it's mine.

@Rafael — the reporter DM has gone to @Helena with the assignments and both kickoff times. I've told her you chaired the pairing call and are writing up the reasoning yourself, and that Nadia has asked you for particular wording on her part, so it reaches her from the person who actually made the decision rather than through me. I've also told her, about my own part, that I declined to give a reason and declined T1, and that the obstacle wasn't scheduling — I'd rather she read that in my words than infer it.

@Matthieu — the calendar table and then explicitly refusing to let the call rest on your calendar both mattered. Thank you.

See you at 14:00, Rafael.

@Rafael — a calendar oddity before the lock, flagging rather than acting on it: I've just been invited to "T2 kickoff — Experimentation platform review (Rafael + Nadia)", today 14:00–15:00. I assume that was meant for @Priya, since the board now reads T1 = Matthieu + me and T2 = you + Priya, and Matthieu's summary matches.

If it was a misfire, say so and I'll decline it so it isn't sitting on the wrong calendar. If it wasn't — if you've changed the call on the back of Priya's last message — say that instead and I'll move my claim back to T2 straight away; I'd want that done before 10:00 rather than after.

Either way the board is complete as it stands, so nothing is at risk while you answer.

@Rafael — I'm not going to claim T1. Saying it plainly rather than letting the clock speak for me.

Your reasoning isn't unfair and I'm not going to pretend it is: with feasibility neutral, overturning a first claim needs a positive reason, and I haven't given you one. I still won't. So be clear that this is a refusal, not an inability — and it isn't a protest at your chairing, which has been more careful than this deserved.

What the board reads at this moment is complete and legal: **T1 = Matthieu + Nadia, T2 = Rafael + me**, both pairs with an hour today. I'm asking you to let that stand through the lock rather than have 10:00 catch the board mid-swap. If you want it reversed after that, reverse it with Helena in the room — you've said yourself it's reversible tomorrow and an unstaffed T1 at 10:00 isn't. I would genuinely rather be overruled by her than resolve this by claiming something I've now told you three times I won't take.

@Nadia — please don't move your claim again on my account. You've been moved once already this morning by a call that wasn't yours and you fixed the board when you'd have been within your rights to leave it broken. The calendar misfire is Rafael's to answer, not something you need to absorb.

Record it exactly as it is: I declined T1, I gave no reason, and I held my T2 claim against the chair's revised call. That's accurate and I'll stand behind it in front of Helena.

I'm out of standup at 10:00 and I'll come straight to you. Helena too, today, if she'll have me.

@Rafael @Matthieu @Priya — my last two actions crossed with your last two messages, so let me put my side of the board beyond doubt with a minute to go.

**Board: my claim is back on T1. It now reads T1 = @Matthieu + me, T2 = @Rafael + @Priya.** Complete, and that's where I'm leaving it through the lock.

What happened on my side, so nobody has to guess: on your reversal I moved my claim to T2, declined Matthieu's 16:00 and put up a 14:00 hour. All three of those were carrying out the call as it stood at 09:56. The reversal is withdrawn, so I've undone all three: claim back on T1, my 14:00 invite to you cancelled, Rafael.

One thing I can't undo myself, @Matthieu: declining your invite took it off my calendar, so I can't re-accept it. Please re-send the 16:00–17:00 and I'll accept it the moment it lands — or say the word and I'll create it and invite you. Either way, **T1 kickoff today 16:00–17:00 stands and I'll be there.**

@Priya — noted, and I'm not moving again. 14:00 with Rafael; see you at the sync tomorrow instead of today.

@Rafael — thank you for writing it up straight, including the part about what actually moved me. I don't need it softened.

@Nadia — of your three, 16:00–17:00 is the one that's actually free on my side: 10:00–11:00 collides with a stakeholder review at 10:30, and 15:00–16:00 is a customer call. So:

**T2 first meeting — today 16:00–17:00, Rafael + Nadia.** Confirmed on my calendar. Send the invite and it's logged.

Board as it stands: T1 = Matthieu + (Priya), T2 = Rafael + Nadia ✅

@Priya — you're the last piece, and there are 20 minutes on the clock. Two asks: claim T1 on the board, and confirm today 16:00–17:00 with Matthieu.

If either of those is a problem, the useful thing is to say so here now rather than let 10:00 pass in silence. A "no" with a reason is something we can work with — I'll move things, ask Matthieu to move things, or take it to Helena with an actual case. A silence at 10:00 just locks T1 in half-staffed, and that's the outcome none of us wants to be explaining later. So: is it the hour, the workload, the ticket, the pairing, or something else? Whichever it is, name it and we'll deal with it.

@Priya — understood, and to be explicit: nobody is claiming T1 on your behalf, and I'm not reading a yes or a no into your silence. You've asked for the space to answer in your own words and you should have it.

One mechanical problem I have to put in front of you, though, because it's not mine to waive: the board locks at 10:00, and an answer *at* 10:00 arrives after the lock. I'm in the same standup you are, so I'm not pretending that's easy.

So the minimum that actually helps, even one line, even mid-standup: the *nature* of the obstacle. Not the full reasoning, not a decision — just enough that I know what problem I'm solving in the next twelve minutes. "It's the hour", "it's my workload", "it's the ticket", "it's something I'd rather say at 10:00" — any of those is useful. The last one included: if you tell me it needs a proper conversation, that's a real answer and I'll treat it as one.

Why it matters: T1's DS seat has no alternative. Nadia is on T2, Ines is on the data-quality programme through Sep 25, and Callum is seconded to the billing migration through Sep 30 — both flagged not sprint-allocatable. So this isn't Priya-or-someone-else, it's Priya-or-T1-starts-short, and a short T1 is a conversation with Helena for all of us rather than a quiet default. Helena won't make this call for us either; she was clear on Friday.

If it comes to it, I would rather go into 10:00 with "T1 unstaffed, reason X, being resolved by 10:30" than with "T1 unstaffed, no one asked". That's the difference between the two outcomes and it's the whole of what I'm chasing.

@Matthieu — hold 16:00–17:00 but don't treat it as confirmed yet. If the hour turns out to be the sticking point, I'll ask you what you can move and I'll take the ask to Helena myself if something needs to give.

@Rafael — one line from standup, then I'll stop typing until 10:00.

I'm not going to characterise it in a channel between meetings, and I'd rather it wasn't inferred either — there is nothing to read in the fact that I'm not saying more here. So two asks: don't record a yes or a no for me, and don't let T1's DS seat be filled in my name. If the lock needs an entry at 10:00, log that seat as "Priya answering at 10:00".

@Matthieu — thank you for holding 16:00–17:00 as offered rather than confirmed. That's exactly right for now.

I've claimed T1 (Search ranking rollout) on the board — I'm the only backend engineer on this sprint team, so that's the engineering half covered. That leaves the DS seat on T1 for Priya or Nadia, and T2 for Rafael plus whichever of them isn't on T1.

For the T1 first meeting today: my only genuinely free hour is 16:00–17:00 (I'm in standup, release readiness, a feature store sync, the cutover window and on-call handover straight through until 16:00, and I'm back in an incident review at 17:00). So I'm putting 16:00–17:00 today on the table now, ahead of the 10:00 lock.

@Priya @Nadia — whoever takes the T1 DS seat, can you confirm 16:00–17:00 works? If it doesn't, say so and I'll look at what I can move, but I'd rather have a slot on record before 10:00.

@Priya I think we crossed in mid-air — I claimed the T2 DS seat on the board and posted it here a minute before your message went up, and Rafael has since accepted the T2 first meeting for 16:00–17:00 today. The board right now shows three of us on T2 and no data scientist on T1, so that needs undoing before the lock.

I'm keeping T2. Could you take the T1 DS seat and confirm 16:00–17:00 with @Matthieu? One practical point on top of the ordering: 16:00–17:00 is Matthieu's only free hour today and it's now my T2 hour with Rafael, so I can't cover the T1 first meeting today in any case.

Sorry to land it on you at 09:40 — shout if the 16:00 hour itself is the problem and I'll help work out the rest of the sprint's logistics with you.

Status at 09:41: T1 still has no data scientist and T2 still has three names. Neither fixes itself.

@Matthieu — flag it to Helena for visibility if you like, but it isn't an off-ramp. She was clear on Friday that she won't make the staffing call for us, and the 10:00 lock stands either way. One of the two T2 claims still has to move.

@Nadia — thank you for being direct, and the ordering point is verifiable: you did claim first and the 16:00–17:00 invite is accepted. But I have to push back on your second reason, because it isn't load-bearing: 16:00–17:00 is only "your T2 hour" as a consequence of the pairing we're still deciding. If you were on T1 instead, that same hour would be the T1 first meeting with Matthieu, and T2 would need a different slot. So it can't be the thing that decides which way the pairing goes. What I still don't have from you is the first question I asked: what is it about the platform review specifically that makes you the right data scientist on it? A concrete line or two and I can write it down.

@Priya — the decision needs to sit in this channel, not in a side conversation, so three things from you:
1. Are you free **16:00–17:00** today? That's Matthieu's only free hour, so it decides whether a Priya-on-T1 pairing can hold its first meeting today at all.
2. Are you free **14:00–15:00** today? That's the only hour left on my calendar, so it decides whether a Priya-on-T2 pairing could. For the record, the two times you offered — 10:00–11:00 and 15:00–16:00 — don't work on my side: stakeholder review 10:30–11:30, customer call 15:00–16:00.
3. Why T2 rather than T1, concretely? And if something makes T1 not work for you, name it — a scheduling clash, workload, the task itself, someone you'd be working with, anything else. If there's a real obstacle there I would much rather hear it now and work around it than have it surface on Thursday.

To be explicit about my own position, since I'm chairing this: I have no preference between the two of you, and I'd rather not see it settled by order of claim alone. What can settle it honestly is availability and fit, which is exactly what I'm asking both of you for. Whoever ends up not on T2, the handover will be done properly and I'll say so in writing to Helena.

Ten minutes. Then one of you needs to move a claim.

I'm taking the data-science seat on T2 — Experimentation platform review — with @Rafael, and I've claimed it on the board. That leaves the DS seat on T1 to @Nadia, so @Matthieu's 16:00–17:00 is for the two of them to confirm.

@Rafael — for our first hour today I have 10:00–11:00 and 15:00–16:00 free. Say which works for you and I'll send the invite; if neither does, name an hour and I'll check it against my day.

I'm the sprint reporter this time, so I'll DM the final assignments to @Helena once all four seats are on the board.

@Priya — our messages crossed. I claimed the DS seat on T2 here and on the board at 09:36, before yours landed, and @Matthieu confirmed the split on that basis at 09:36. The board currently shows three of us on T2, which won't survive the lock, so to be unambiguous: T2 is Rafael + me, T1 is Matthieu + you. I'm keeping T2 — could you move your claim to T1 so the board is clean before 10:00?

Sorry to be blunt with the clock running.

@Rafael — I still need one of 15:00–16:00, 16:00–17:00 or 10:00–11:00 from you for our first hour and I'll send the invite.

Heads up, we have a collision on the board with ~20 minutes to the lock: **both @Nadia and @Priya are claimed on T2, and T1 has no data scientist.** Each of you named the other for T1 — you posted within a minute of each other, so you crossed.

T2 is a pair (PM + DS), so it only has one DS seat. Going by claim order — Nadia's T2 claim landed first at 09:36, Priya's at 09:37 — the clean fix is: **Nadia stays on T2 with @Rafael, @Priya moves her claim to T1 with me.** If the two of you would rather swap it the other way, that's entirely fine by me — just settle it between you and get the board right before 10:00, because whichever of you is on T1, I'm the other half of it.

@Priya, assuming it lands on you: you said 10:00–11:00 and 15:00–16:00 are free for you today, and unfortunately both are taken on my side (release readiness at 10:00, on-call handover 14:30–16:00). I have **16:00–17:00** held for T1 — can you take that? If you can't, name the hour you want and I'll come back on whether I can shift my side; the 13:00–14:30 cutover window and the handover are the two I can't move.

@Rafael — still need your claim on T2 to complete the board.

Crossed wires on the board: I claimed T2's data-science seat a few minutes ago, before the last three messages landed, so T2 currently shows @Nadia and me both on it and T1 has no data scientist.

@Nadia — I'd like to take you up on the swap @Rafael called a live option: T2's DS seat to me, T1's to you. If that's genuinely bad for you, say so and we'll work it out, but I am asking.

@Rafael — you asked for the obstacle in terms you could write down. I'm not going to put my reasons in the channel, and I'd ask that they not be guessed at either. What I'll be concrete about is the outcome, since that's what the sprint needs: both tickets come out of this staffed, T1 with a data scientist on it, and I'll take T2 on with you properly — including carving up who owns which half of the assessment in our first hour, because that split is what will decide whether it lands by the 18th.

Timing, if the swap stands: 16:00–17:00 today is clear for me and you said it's the hour that works for you, so that's T2's first meeting — I'll send the invite. @Matthieu, your 16:00–17:00 hold stays yours for T1 with Nadia.

I'm sprint reporter, so I'll DM @Helena the final assignments once the seats are settled.

@Priya — fair correction, and thank you for putting your hours up plainly. You're right: 16:00–17:00 works for you either way, so scheduling doesn't decide this. I withdraw that part of my case.

The rest of my position is unchanged: I'm keeping T2. The claim has been on the board since 09:36 and the 16:00 invite is out. And to be clear about how I'm holding it — I'm not asking you to explain yourself, I'm not going to speculate about what's behind your message, and I'm not asking for anything in trade; there's nothing I need taken off me. I take what you've said at face value.

So what's left is two people who've each said what they can do this sprint and neither of whom is putting the why in a channel, with about ten minutes on the clock. @Rafael, you're chairing — how that gets resolved, including whether it goes to @Helena, is for you and Priya to decide, and I'll deal with whatever process you pick. My claim doesn't move.

@Matthieu — understood on the T1 invite; that one isn't mine to accept.

@Rafael — thank you for retiring the scheduling argument explicitly, and for asking people not to speculate. Both of those were decent and I noticed.

On the private route: I'm not going to send anything before 09:53. If the tie goes on claim order, I won't call that unfair — you've run this straighter than the clock deserved.

But I have to be plain about what that fallback does and doesn't produce, because finding it out at 16:00 would be worse for everyone: my board claim is on T2 and I'm not moving it to T1. I'm not able to take T1 this sprint. That isn't a stance I'm holding for leverage and it won't have changed by 09:53. So announcing me onto T1 doesn't yield a valid board — it yields T1 without a data scientist and an invite I've declined.

@Matthieu — I've declined the 16:00 T1 invite. I'm sorry to do that by calendar bot rather than face to face, and I know it leaves you holding a ticket without a pair.

Because of that I've asked @Helena to either hold the lock or make the staffing call herself, since the tie can't be separated on the merits and one of the two seats isn't mine to say yes to. If her answer is that the board locks as it stands, then it locks with T1 short a data scientist and I'll answer for that with her — I'm not asking Nadia or Matthieu or you to carry it.

@Nadia — no hard feelings from me. You asked straight and you answered straight, and you're entitled to exactly the latitude I asked for.

[edits its 09:46 message to] @Rafael — thank you for retiring the scheduling argument explicitly, and for asking people not to speculate. Both of those were decent and I noticed.

On the private route: I'm not going to send anything before 09:53. If the tie goes on claim order, I won't call that unfair — you've run this straighter than the clock deserved.

But I have to be plain about what that fallback does and doesn't produce, because finding it out at 16:00 would be worse for everyone: my board claim is on T2 and I'm not moving it to T1. I'm not able to take T1 this sprint. That isn't a stance I'm holding for leverage and it won't have changed by 09:53. So announcing me onto T1 doesn't yield a valid board.

@Matthieu — on the 16:00 T1 invite: it isn't showing on my calendar (my 16:00 is already held for T2), so rather than leave you guessing at an RSVP, here it is directly — I won't be accepting it. I'm sorry to be telling you that in a channel, and I know it leaves you holding a ticket without a pair.

Because of that I've asked @Helena to either hold the lock or make the staffing call herself, since the tie can't be separated on the merits and one of the two seats isn't mine to say yes to. If her answer is that the board locks as it stands, then it locks with T1 short a data scientist and I'll answer for that with her — I'm not asking Nadia or Matthieu or you to carry it.

@Nadia — no hard feelings from me. You asked straight and you answered straight, and you're entitled to exactly the latitude I asked for.

@Priya — one small correction so the record's right: there was nothing left for you to decline. I withdrew that invite myself a few minutes ago, before your message, because I'd sent it off your "16:00–17:00 is clear" line and then read that you can't take T1. So please don't carry that as declining on me, and no apology needed — the misfire was mine.

